### 4.0 Worked example · gates · null check

**One decision (N100|SC100, window 52, exit E1).** On 2007-03-02 the plain ratio N100 ÷ SC100 closed at 1.1790 against a trailing-52-week mean of 1.2246 and sd 0.0316: below mean − 1 sd, so N100 is the lagging leg → target A. The trade happened on 2007-03-05 at fills N100 3474.97 / SC100 2905.26; cost 0.001018 of NAV. The position closed on the decision of 2007-03-23 (exit: back at the mean), traded 2007-03-26: the held leg returned +7.21% fill to fill against the peer's +3.12% — extra +4.09%.

**One path.** NAV 1.000 on 2006-10-20 → 4.290 on 2026-08-28: CAGR 7.61%, worst fall -72.2%.

**One draw (N-A, draw 0).** The same 27 trade spells scattered at random: CAGR 14.16%. **One ranking.** The strategy's 7.61% sits at the 11.5th percentile of 2,000 draws (p = 0.885); the null's median is 10.00%, edge -2.39%.

| gate | result | evidence |
|---|---|---|
| V1 independent verifier | PASS | band on P_a / P_b (audit: plain), maximum hold None (None = no cap); 100 nav files, 61230 comparisons, 0 failures; corrupted copies caught |
| V2 no look-ahead | PASS | 8,827,882 point-in-time checks, 0 violations |
| V3 null held its promise | PASS | 400,000 draws checked, 0 with different counts |
| V4 regression | PASS | always-neutral sleeve = 50/50 buy-and-hold closed form: yes; the changed engine reproduces T02 (final NAV, CAGR, max dd within 1e-9): 600 of 600 rows of tests/T02/evidence/headline/summary.csv, and T01: 600 of 600 rows of tests/T01/evidence/headline/summary.csv |

**Null check.** Every one of the 400,000 draws kept the strategy's number of spells, switches and weeks in each state (measured, not assumed): yes.

