### 4.3 How much evidence, and the MDE

Independent observations are round trips, not weeks: N100 ÷ MC100 26 round trips over 1037 weeks, N100 ÷ SC100 27 round trips over 1037 weeks, N100 ÷ Micro250 6 round trips over 201 weeks, MC100 ÷ SC100 35 round trips over 1037 weeks, MC100 ÷ Micro250 8 round trips over 201 weeks, SC100 ÷ Micro250 5 round trips over 201 weeks.

Next to every FAIL above, the smallest edge the test could have seen (2.8 × the null's sd of CAGR): N100 ÷ MC100 undetectable below 3.1 pp a year, N100 ÷ SC100 undetectable below 5.4 pp a year, N100 ÷ Micro250 undetectable below 12.1 pp a year, MC100 ÷ SC100 undetectable below 2.8 pp a year, MC100 ÷ Micro250 undetectable below 8.6 pp a year, SC100 ÷ Micro250 undetectable below 4.0 pp a year. A FAIL means 'too small to see', not 'nothing there'.

